	(text "J1 is soldered on the BOTTOM side.\nPin numbers match the watch's J4:\n1 GND  3 SDA  5 AUX (3.3 V, awake)\n2 3V3  4 SCL  6 AIN (audio in)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 88.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e957f50f-2561-5290-b225-eb81fe98cbae")
	)
	(text "Order V G SCL SDA, as on most cheap\nI2C boards (BME280, BH1750, AHT20,\nGY-521). Many OLED boards swap V and G\n(G V SCL SDA): check before soldering."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 96.52 88.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "45d565a8-7bc3-572c-b646-a037bdf015e0")
	)
	(text "MAX4466 / MAX9814: OUT, VCC, GND.\nVCC is AUX, so the microphone is\noff while the watch sleeps."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 88.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d6ab8b7c-5820-5b3f-b1be-6ac54e5a18c0")
	)
	(text "Qwiic pinout: 1 GND, 2 3V3, 3 SDA, 4 SCL.\nMP = the two metal tabs, solder only."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 152.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8a75a286-62ca-52b1-b4f5-149bce9d82d9")
	)
	(text "Pads 1-2 bridged at the factory: PWR = 3V3 (always on).\nCut that bridge and blob 2-3: PWR = AUX (on only while the\nwatch is awake) - for modules with a power LED, MPU6050..."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 96.52 152.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "96cc3a65-b7c9-5657-8022-c8cd44f06dac")
	)
